  "question": {
    "text": "In a typical combustion engine the workdone by a gas molecule is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is the displacement, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is the Boltzmann constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is the temperature. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are constants, dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> will be:"
  },
